# Copy this file to .env and fill in the values you have. Every value is
# optional — the app runs fully in Demo Mode with zero configuration.
#
# SECURITY: every variable in this file is safe to ship inside the compiled
# mobile app (that's what EXPO_PUBLIC_ means — Expo inlines these into the
# JS bundle at build time, so anyone can extract them from the app binary).
# Never add a secret key here. AI provider keys and the Supabase
# service-role key belong in Supabase Edge Function secrets or your own
# server environment instead — see supabase/functions/.env.example and the
# "AI provider setup" section of README.md for exactly where those go and
# why.

# --- Supabase (client-safe) ------------------------------------------------
# Leave both blank to run in Demo Mode (local on-device storage, seeded with
# a demo user "Alex"). Fill in both to use a real backend. The anon key is
# meant to be public — it identifies your project, not a privileged
# credential — access control is enforced by Postgres Row Level Security
# (see supabase/migrations/), not by keeping this key secret.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# --- Local dev/CLI scripts only — never used by the app itself ------------
# These are read by scripts/run-migrations.js, scripts/run-seed.js, and
# scripts/generate-audio.ts, which all run on your own machine via `npm
# run ...`, never inside the compiled app. Do not add the EXPO_PUBLIC_
# prefix to any of these — that prefix is what causes a variable to be
# bundled into the client app, which must never happen to a secret.
#
# Project Settings > Database > Connection string (URI).
DATABASE_URL=
# Project Settings > API > service_role key. Used only by scripts/run-seed.js
# to create the demo auth user server-side.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
# `npm run audio:generate` (pre-rendering listening-test audio) uses the
# local, free Piper TTS engine — no API key needed. It requires `pip install
# piper-tts`, `python3 -m piper.download_voices --data-dir .piper-voices
# en_GB-vctk-medium`, and `ffmpeg` on your machine. See README.md's
# "Listening audio pipeline" section for the full setup and the Piper/VCTK
# license attribution this requires. The app works without any of this —
# every shipped listening track already has bundled audio; on-device TTS is
# only a last-resort fallback for a track with no bundled audio at all.
# Optional overrides, only read by scripts/generate-audio.ts:
# PIPER_VOICE=en_GB-vctk-medium
# PIPER_VOICE_DIR=.piper-voices

# --- RevenueCat (subscriptions, client-safe) --------------------------------
# These are RevenueCat's PUBLIC SDK keys (Project settings > API keys >
# "Public app-specific API keys" in the RevenueCat dashboard — safe to ship,
# they identify your app to RevenueCat and don't grant access to anything by
# themselves). RevenueCat's SEPARATE secret/admin API key must never go
# here, or anywhere in this repo — it's only ever needed for RevenueCat's
# own server-side REST API, which this app doesn't call at all (see
# "RevenueCat setup" in README.md for why the webhook-based sync design
# avoids ever needing it).
#
# Leaving both blank behaves differently depending on whether Supabase is
# configured above: with no Supabase project (Demo Mode), the paywall runs
# fully simulated purchases for demoing the UI. With a REAL Supabase project
# but no RevenueCat key, the paywall instead shows "subscriptions aren't
# available yet" and refuses to let anything "purchase" — a real account
# must never be granted a fabricated Premium subscription just because
# RevenueCat isn't wired up yet. See "RevenueCat / Google Play Billing
# setup" in README.md for exactly what to create in Play Console and
# RevenueCat, and the Android product ids this app expects.
EXPO_PUBLIC_REVENUECAT_IOS_KEY=
EXPO_PUBLIC_REVENUECAT_ANDROID_KEY=
